module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.ResolutionOfSurfaces.RationalDoublePoints.ChartPoint

/-!
# The chart ring of a blowup of an affine spectrum, read over the ring

The coordinate ring `AlgebraicGeometry.blowupChartRing` of a standard affine chart of a blowup is
the affine blowup algebra of the ideal of *sections* of the centre on an affine open. On the
spectrum of a ring `A` with the open taken to be the whole space, that ideal lives in
`Γ(Spec A, ⊤)` rather than in `A`, so the chart ring is an affine blowup algebra over
`Γ(Spec A, ⊤)` while every statement proved about the affine blowup algebra of an ideal of `A` —
its presentation, its normalization — is over `A`. This file crosses between the two along the
canonical isomorphism `Γ(Spec A, ⊤) ≅ A`.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.mem_ideal_ofIdealTop_isAffineOpen_top`: the image of an element of an
  ideal `J` of `A` is a section of the ideal sheaf `J` generates, which is the datum
  `AlgebraicGeometry.blowupChartRing` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.PointBlowupStage.exists_next_of_chart` take.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.exists_ringEquiv_blowupChartRing_ofIdealTop`: **the chart ring over the whole
  space of `Spec A` is the affine blowup algebra over `A`**, by an isomorphism commuting with the
  structure maps from the base.

## Implementation notes

The transport of the affine blowup algebra itself is
`Stacks.Blowup.exists_ringEquiv_affineBlowupAlgebra'` of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/MoreMorphisms/CoordinateBlowupSmooth.lean`, which takes an
isomorphism of base rings together with a compatible isomorphism of the localizations. Here the
base isomorphism is `Γ(Spec A, ⊤) ≅ A` and the compatible isomorphism of localizations is
`IsLocalization.ringEquivOfRingEquiv`, the submonoid condition being `Submonoid.map_powers`. The
primed form of the transport is the one used because the ideal and the element on the
`Γ(Spec A, ⊤)` side arrive as the sections of an ideal sheaf, that is up to equality rather than
as literal images.

The compatibility recorded in the conclusion is with the structure maps from the base, and not
only with the inclusions into the localizations: the three conditions of
`AlgebraicGeometry.PointBlowupStage.exists_next_of_chart` which concern the chart ring — that the
chosen prime is maximal, that it contracts to the prime of the centre, and that the sections over
the open generate the quotient there — are all statements about
`algebraMap Γ(Spec A, ⊤) (blowupChartRing …)`, so that is the map which has to be transported.

That the sections over the whole space of `Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop K` are `K` is
`simp`, and is also stated twice in the library already —
`AlgebraicGeometry.ofIdealTop_ideal_top` in `FormalGeometry/CoherentAdicSystem/Equivalence.lean`
and `AlgebraicGeometry.ideal_top_ofIdealTop` in `Spaces/LocallyPrincipalChartScheme.lean`, which
are the same statement in two modules. It is used here as a `have` rather than by importing
either, so that no third copy enters the library and neither of those heavy modules is pulled
into this one's import closure. Unifying that pre-existing pair is a separate job.

No `@[stacks]` attribute is attached. [Stacks, Tag 052Q] is registered on the affine blowup
algebra in `StacksFrontier/RingTheory/Blowup/Defs.lean` and [Stacks, Tag 0804] on the chart
identification in `Blowup/ReesAlgebra/AffineCharts.lean`; what is here is the comparison of two
spellings of one ring and formalizes no tag.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 052Q](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/052Q)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0804](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0804)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory TopologicalSpace

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-- **An element of an ideal of a ring is a section of the ideal sheaf it generates on the
spectrum.** The image under `A ≅ Γ(Spec A, ⊤)` of an element of `J` is a section over the whole
space of the ideal sheaf generated by the image of `J`.

This supplies the section `a` which `AlgebraicGeometry.blowupChartRing` and
`AlgebraicGeometry.PointBlowupStage.exists_next_of_chart` take, from an element of an ideal of
the ring. -/
public theorem mem_ideal_ofIdealTop_isAffineOpen_top (A : Type u) [CommRing A] (J : Ideal A)
    {b : A} (hb : b ∈ J) :
    (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of A)).inv.hom b ∈
      (Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop
        (J.map (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of A)).inv.hom)).ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩ := by
  simpa using Ideal.mem_map_of_mem (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of A)).inv.hom hb

/-- **The chart ring over the whole space of `Spec A` is the affine blowup algebra over `A`.**
Let `J` be an ideal of `A` and `b ∈ A`, and let `a` be a section over the whole space of the ideal
sheaf generated by the image of `J` whose value is the image of `b`. Then the coordinate ring
`Γ(Spec A, ⊤)[J/a]` of the standard chart attached to `a` is isomorphic to the affine blowup
algebra `A[J/b]`, by an isomorphism commuting with the structure maps from the base along
`A ≅ Γ(Spec A, ⊤)`.

This is the bridge between the statements proved about the affine blowup algebra of an ideal of
`A` and the chart ring of the blowup of `Spec A`, which is what
`AlgebraicGeometry.PointBlowupStage.exists_next_of_chart` consumes. The section `a` is supplied
by `AlgebraicGeometry.mem_ideal_ofIdealTop_isAffineOpen_top`, with which the hypothesis `ha` is
`rfl`. -/
public theorem exists_ringEquiv_blowupChartRing_ofIdealTop (A : Type u) [CommRing A]
    (J : Ideal A) (b : A)
    (a : ↥((Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop
      (J.map (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of A)).inv.hom)).ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩))
    (ha : (a : Γ(Spec (.of A), ⊤)) = (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of A)).inv.hom b) :
    ∃ E : affineBlowupAlgebra J b (Localization.Away b) ≃+*
        blowupChartRing (Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop
          (J.map (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of A)).inv.hom)) ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩ a,
      ∀ x : A,
        E (algebraMap A (affineBlowupAlgebra J b (Localization.Away b)) x) =
          algebraMap Γ(Spec (.of A), ⊤)
            (blowupChartRing (Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop
              (J.map (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of A)).inv.hom)) ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩ a)
            ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of A)).inv.hom x) := by
  set ψ : A ≃+* Γ(Spec (.of A), ⊤) :=
    (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of A)).commRingCatIsoToRingEquiv.symm
  have hψb : ψ b = (a : Γ(Spec (.of A), ⊤)) := ha.symm
  have H : (Submonoid.powers b).map ψ.toMonoidHom =
      Submonoid.powers (a : Γ(Spec (.of A), ⊤)) := by
    rw [Submonoid.map_powers]
    exact congrArg Submonoid.powers hψb
  let Λ : Localization.Away b ≃+* Localization.Away (a : Γ(Spec (.of A), ⊤)) :=
    IsLocalization.ringEquivOfRingEquiv _ _ ψ H
  have hΛ : ∀ x : A, Λ (algebraMap A (Localization.Away b) x) =
      algebraMap Γ(Spec (.of A), ⊤) (Localization.Away (a : Γ(Spec (.of A), ⊤))) (ψ x) :=
    IsLocalization.ringEquivOfRingEquiv_eq H
  obtain ⟨E, hE⟩ := Stacks.Blowup.exists_ringEquiv_affineBlowupAlgebra' ψ Λ b J
    ((Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop
      (J.map (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of A)).inv.hom)).ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩)
    (a : Γ(Spec (.of A), ⊤)) hΛ (by simp; rfl) hψb.symm
  exact ⟨E, fun x => Subtype.ext ((hE _).trans (hΛ x))⟩

end AlgebraicGeometry

end
